# The Spec 026-034 audit chain pins file bytes with SHA-256: reviewed-artifact
# manifests, source-bundle manifests, predecessor digests, and the pinned
# upstream bundle are all hashed verbatim. This repository is authored on
# Windows (CRLF) while `core.autocrlf=input` stores LF, so a clone that checks
# out LF -- exactly the WSL/Linux host the Hermes runbook requires -- would
# change those bytes and invalidate every digest. The failure surfaces as
# BLOCKED_SOURCE_GRAPH and dozens of audit-test failures that look like a
# security regression rather than an end-of-line conversion.
#
# Keep every digest-pinned surface byte-identical on all platforms.
